<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhai Liao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 391</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingling">Dingling</a> chieftain who founded the Zhai Wei state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> during the break-up of the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>. After serving and turning on several powers in turn, he proclaimed himself Heavenly King of Wei in 388. He died in 391, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhai-zhao">Zhai Zhao</a> lost the state to the Later Yan in 392.</p></div>
